  "generated_text": "To find \\( g(4) \\), we need to understand how the functions \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) are related. We are given that \\( f(x) = 2x - 3 \\) and \\( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \\). This means that when we input \\( f(x) \\) into \\( g \\), we get \\( 5 - 4x \\).\n\nFirst, let's determine the value of \\( x \\) such that \\( f(x) = 4 \\). We set up the equation:\n\\[\nf(x) = 2x - 3 = 4\n\\]\nSolving for \\( x \\), we get:\n\\[\n2x - 3 = 4 \\implies 2x = 7 \\implies x = \\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\nSo, \\( f\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) = 4 \\). This tells us that \\( g(4) = g(f\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)) = 5 - 4\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) \\).\n\nNow, we simplify \\( 5 - 4\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) \\):\n\\[\n5 - 4\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) = 5 - 2 \\cdot 7 = 5 - 14 = -9\n\\]\nTherefore, \\( g(4) = -9 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-9}\n\\]",
